==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|modifien}}, from {{der|en|frm|modifier}}, from {{der|en|la|modificare||to limit, control, regulate, deponent}}, from {{m|la|modificari||to measure off, set bound to, moderate}}, from {{m|la|modus||measure}} + {{m|la|facere||to make}}; see {{m|en|mode}}.
{{root|en|ine-pro|*dʰeh₁-}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈmɒdɪfaɪ/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈmɑdɪfaɪ/|a=GA}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-modify.ogg|a=US}}
* {{hyph|en|mod|i|fy}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[change]] [[part]] of.
#: {{ux|en|Her publisher advised her to '''modify''' a few parts of the book to make it easier to read.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To be or become modified.
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To set bounds to; to [[moderate]].
# {{lb|en|transitive|grammar}} To [[qualify]] the [[meaning]] of.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1977|author=Linda R. Waugh|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=NckUAAAAIAAJ&pg=PA156&dq=adjectives+modify&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwj-kr-SqLLiAhUHPK0KHYJyAxsQ6AEIQjAE#v=onepage&q=adjectives%20modify&f=false|title=A Semantic Analysis of Word Order: Position of the Adjective in French|text=There is inherently no ordering to the modification and no hierarchy of modification: that is, both adjectives '''modify''' the substantive and both apply equally to the substantive{{...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2016|author=Allen Ascher|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=vs25DQAAQBAJ&pg=PA192&dq=nouns+modify&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwiG5bzgqLLiAhUBbKwKHSa0DLYQ6AEIRjAF#v=onepage&q=nouns%20modify&f=false|title=The New Harbrace Guide: Genres for Composing|text=Adjectives '''modify''' nouns.}}

